        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Barcelona</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 15 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Settlement on the site is older than 5000 BCE; the Laietani, an Iberian people, held Barkeno in the 3rd and 2nd centuries BCE, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> redrew the town as a castrum about 15 BCE. Founding by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca">Hamilcar Barca</a> or by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hercules-kassel">Hercules</a> is legend.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On a coastal plain about 5 km wide on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, between the Collserola range and the sea, and between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llobregat">Llobregat</a> river to the south-west and the Besòs river to the north.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Roman colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcino">Barcino</a>; a Visigothic royal seat; the County of Barcelona and the Crown of Aragon; a medieval trading port with a large Jewish community; the 1714 siege; the Eixample; Gaudí and Catalan modernisme; the Spanish Civil War; the Olympic Games of 1992</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Barcelona is the capital of the autonomous community of Catalonia and the second largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</span></div>
